InteliBin — Smart Waste Bin Monitoring System
University of Zambia — Final Year Project
An IoT-enabled smart waste bin that measures fill level using an ultrasonic sensor,
automates the lid via a servo motor, and displays real-time data on a web dashboard.

Project Structure
C:/xampp/htdocs/intelibin/
│
├── dashboard.php               Main monitoring dashboard (live fill level, chart, log)
├── bins.php                    View all bins, fill level, and last emptied time
├── history.php                 Filterable table of all past sensor readings
├── settings.php                Configure bin name, location, and height
├── about.php                   System overview, pipeline diagram, hardware specs
│
├── assets/
│   └── css/
│       └── app.css             Shared styles used across all pages
│
├── includes/
│   ├── db.php                  MySQL connection — edit credentials here
│   ├── header.php              Shared navigation bar and page head
│   └── footer.php              Shared footer
│
├── api/
│   ├── fetch_latest.php        GET  — returns latest bin reading as JSON
│   └── command.php             POST — sends open/close/reset command to bin
│
├── arduino/
│   └── intelibin/
│       └── intelibin.ino       Arduino sketch — upload to board via Arduino IDE
│
├── python/
│   └── serial_to_mysql.py      Runs on PC — reads USB serial, writes to MySQL
│
└── sql/
    ├── intelibin_db.sql         Import this FIRST in phpMyAdmin
    └── intelibin_twoway.sql     Import this SECOND in phpMyAdmin

Hardware
Controller: Arduino Uno R3
USB: Arduino Uno connects directly to the PC. USB provides power and serial communication at 9600 baud.
Person detection sensor: HC-SR04, TRIG D9, ECHO D10, VCC 5V, GND GND. Detection threshold: about 15 cm.
Fill level sensor: HC-SR04, TRIG D4, ECHO D5, VCC 5V, GND GND. Uses median of 7 readings.
Fill calibration: empty = 20.9 cm, full = 4.0 cm.
Servo: signal D6, red 5V, brown GND, orange D6. Closed = 90 degrees, open = 180 degrees.

Setup
1. Database

Open http://localhost/phpmyadmin
Create a new database named intelibin (done)
Import sql/intelibin_db.sql first
Import sql/intelibin_twoway.sql second

2. Web App

Make sure XAMPP Apache and MySQL are both running
Confirm the folder is at C:/xampp/htdocs/intelibin/
Open includes/db.php and check these lines match your setup:

phpdefine('DB_HOST', 'localhost');
define('DB_NAME', 'intelibin');
define('DB_PORT', 3307);
define('DB_USER', 'root');
define('DB_PASS', '');  // blank if no MySQL password set

Visit http://localhost/intelibin/dashboard.php

3. Arduino

Open arduino/intelibin/intelibin.ino in Arduino IDE
Select board: Arduino Uno
Select the correct COM port (e.g. COM3)
Click Upload
Leave the Arduino plugged in via USB

4. Python Script
Install dependencies (run once):
pip install pyserial pymysql
Open python/serial_to_mysql.py and confirm these match your setup:
pythonSERIAL_PORT = 'COM3'    # match the COM port your Arduino is on
BIN_HEIGHT  = 30        # cm — physical height of your bin
Run the script:
python python/serial_to_mysql.py
Keep this running whenever the system is active. It bridges the Arduino and the database.

How It Works
HC-SR04 Sensor
     ↓
Arduino Uno  (reads distance, detects person, controls servo lid)
     ↓  USB Serial
Python Script  (python/serial_to_mysql.py — receives readings, sends commands)
     ↓
MySQL Database  (stores readings, manages alerts, queues commands)
     ↓
PHP API  (fetch_latest.php, command.php)
     ↓
Web Dashboard  (polls every 30 seconds, updates without page reload)

Fill Level Thresholds
RangeStatusColourAlert0% – 19%ReadyGreenNo20% – 49%FillingBlueNo50% – 79%Almost FullAmberNo80% – 100%FullRedYes

Serial Protocol
Messages the Arduino sends to the PC are newline-delimited JSON:
{"event":"reading","personDistance":35.2,"fillDistance":8.4,"fillPercentage":74,"lid":"closed"}
{"event":"person","personDistance":12.0,"detected":true,"fillDistance":8.4,"fillPercentage":74,"lid":"open"}
{"event":"lid","personDistance":12.0,"fillDistance":8.4,"fillPercentage":74,"lid":"closed"}
Messages the PC sends to the Arduino:
MessageMeaningOPENOpen the lidCLOSEClose the lid

Remote Lid Control (Operator Flow)

Bin reaches 80% → dashboard shows Full alert
Trash collector notifies operator
Operator opens dashboard → clicks Open Bin
Dashboard calls api/command.php → stores command in MySQL
Python script detects command → sends OPEN to Arduino via serial
Arduino opens lid → sends a JSON lid event back to Python
Python confirms in MySQL → dashboard updates lid status
After emptying, operator clicks Reset → lid closes, bin resets to Ready


